    "body": "> > \r\n> \r\n> Hmm... preconnect doesn't send error events at all. what would be the value in verifying that it doesn't send error events on particular cases?\r\n\r\nWe've historically had some bad interop and spec work around error events, especially for URL parsing issues. (It feels almost random which elements send error events when.) So verifying they aren't sent in this case would help lock things down.",
